course: dictionary
lesson: 5453
title: Landmass: one big piece of land
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A landmass is a very large area of land that is all joined together, with no sea cutting through it. Think of it as one big piece of ground. «Europe and Asia are one landmass, often called Eurasia.» Even though we give Europe and Asia different names, they are joined as one piece of land.
explain: Some landmasses are continents, and some are big islands. «Australia is the smallest continent, with about 7.7 million square kilometres.» Australia is so big on its own that it counts as a continent, not just an island. A small island is not a landmass because it is not very large.
explain: Landmasses are not always split up the way we draw them on maps. «That is a human agreement, like the EU5 designers deciding where one region ends and the next begins.» People decide where Europe ends and Asia begins, but the land itself is one landmass. To check a word like this, ask: is this a very large area of land that is joined together?
fact: A landmass is a very large, continuous area of land.
fact: Eurasia is one landmass made of Europe and Asia.
fact: Australia is the smallest continent, and it is the only continent that is a single country.
fact: Long ago, the landmasses were joined together in one supercontinent called Pangaea.
fact: Landmasses move very slowly over time, which is called plate tectonics.
exercise: What is a landmass? | A type of cloud | A small lake surrounded by water | *A very large area of land that is all joined together | A sea with no land nearby
exercise: «Australia is the smallest continent.» Why is Australia counted as a continent and not just an island? | *Because it is such a big landmass on its own | Because it is made of ice | Because it is in the middle of the Atlantic | Because it has more people than any island
exercise: «Europe and Asia are really one landmass, Eurasia.» Find and copy the word that names a very large joined area of land. | *landmass | Europe | really | Asia
test: Which of these is a landmass? | A drop of rain | A small pond in a park | A lake | *Asia
test: «Europe and Asia are one landmass, often called Eurasia.» What is the name often used for them together? | Pangaea | *Eurasia | Antarctica | Australia
exam: The landmasses of the world move very slowly over time. What is this process called? | Erosion of the sea | *Plate tectonics | Weather | Photosynthesis
